# Claim C4, third manifestation found while reducing: when the
# type()d alias pair lives at the TOP LEVEL of the included file, the
# same pattern dies with a bogus [aontu/mapval_spread_required] "The
# value for key T is required (defined in spread)" — though NO spread
# exists anywhere in either file ("Cannot unify value: integer with
# value: nil").  Inline in one file the same statements emit
# {"customers":{"c1":{"a":5}}}.
# expected: {"customers":{"c1":{"a":5}}} exit 0
# actual:   [aontu/mapval_spread_required] at $.T, exit 1 (bogus error)
@"./alias-top.aon"
customers: c1: $.C & { a: 5 }
